{"id": "EUVD-2026-104687", "enisaUuid": "d79279aa-674a-35e0-bcc9-0d8145180e12", "description": "EvoScientist 0.1.0 before 0.2.5 contains an approval bypass vulnerability that allows attackers to run host shell commands by delegating them to async sub-agents lacking an interrupt_on gate. Attackers can plant instructions in ingested content such as fetched web pages, so the agent calls start_async_task and runs commands with user privileges and environment secrets.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T00:46:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T21:09:21", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://www.lasso.security/vulnerability-database/cve-2026-77930", "https://github.com/EvoScientist/EvoScientist/issues/387", "https://github.com/EvoScientist/EvoScientist/commit/d249e320bd856a7d31d859cfbb2bf75bab6c8686", "https://github.com/EvoScientist/EvoScientist/releases/tag/v0.2.5", "https://github.com/EvoScientist/EvoScientist/blob/ac58caab7bdd1706f3fee55891f611cd175d05b0/EvoScientist/subagents/_factory.py#L116", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/evoscientist-0.1.0-before-0.2.5-human-approval-bypass-via-async-sub-agents"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-77930", "GHSA-626g-hx6f-fj54"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.44, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a5de1bca-861b-37d3-aa99-af9cd6fcfdeb", "product": {"name": "EvoScientist", "vendor": {"name": "EvoScientist"}}, "product_version": "0.1.0 <0.2.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "28b7f0df-febc-3b98-b3ff-2cb567818c97", "vendor": {"name": "EvoScientist"}}], "isExploited": false}